00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:05.520
US markets closed for Memorial Day while Canadian trading continued amid oil price swings.

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:10.100
Geopolitical tensions around the Strait of Hormuz kept sentiment cautious,

00:01:10.660 --> 00:01:13.480
even as AI chip names lifted the broader indices.

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:20.160
While markets set records, the real story was how investors are rethinking the tools they use to keep up,

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:21.620
starting with AI.

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:27.500
AI-driven analytics are moving from software disruption into core Wall Street functions,

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:30.560
such as research, trading signals, and risk modeling.

00:01:31.220 --> 00:01:35.180
The shift matters now because the same large language model techniques

00:01:35.180 --> 00:01:39.320
already use for sentiment scanning can be applied by retail investors

00:01:39.320 --> 00:01:44.060
to scan earnings, transcripts, or regulatory filings faster than manual review.

00:01:44.860 --> 00:01:49.880
One practical implementation is to feed quarterly reports into an LLM prompt

00:01:49.880 --> 00:01:53.640
that extracts forward-looking statements on margins and capex,

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:57.320
then cross-check those outputs against consensus estimates.

00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:03.720
Retail investors can replicate institutional grade research inside existing brokerage platforms

00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:05.800
without waiting for cell side notes.

00:02:06.440 --> 00:02:10.740
This approach turns hours of manual reading into minutes of structured output

00:02:10.740 --> 00:02:13.080
that highlights sustainable cash flow signals.

00:02:13.880 --> 00:02:18.180
Bank earnings beats paired with dividend hikes offer a concrete income

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:22.760
plus growth setup for TFSA and RRSP accounts.

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:26.760
When capital markets revenue drives the outperformance

00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:31.440
the payout increase signals sustainable cash flow rather than one-time gains.

00:02:32.260 --> 00:02:38.520
Today's BML reports showed net income of $2.6 billion up 34% year-over-year,

00:02:38.980 --> 00:02:41.360
directly tied to trading and advisory fees.

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:47.180
Investors can screen for banks where capital markets revenue exceeds 25% of total

00:02:47.180 --> 00:02:50.300
and the dividend yield sits above the sector average,

00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:54.020
then enter on the post earnings pullback if volume confirms.

00:02:54.800 --> 00:03:02.440
Similar results from TD, RBC, and CIBC showed profits rising between 25% year-over-year at RBC

00:03:02.960 --> 00:03:06.240
and solid beats at the others with all three lifting payouts.

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:12.140
The strategy is to filter TSX listed banks for quarter-over-quarter dividend growth

00:03:12.140 --> 00:03:16.580
above 5% and payout ratios below 60%.

00:03:16.580 --> 00:03:20.440
Income strategies worked yet inflation data complicated the picture.

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:24.660
Tips ETFs are seeing inflows as investors seek inflation protection

00:03:25.240 --> 00:03:29.620
yet the underlying mechanism often fails to deliver when real yields shift

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:32.500
or supply chains adjust faster than CPI.

00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:37.980
The strategy involves buying treasury inflation protected securities through ETFs

00:03:37.980 --> 00:03:39.760
to hedge rising consumer prices,

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:43.400
but the article shows that when inflation hits a three-year high,

00:03:43.880 --> 00:03:46.440
the funds can still post negative real returns.

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:52.040
This highlights the limits of single-factor inflation protection in the current environment.

00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:57.220
When macro data weakens, the filter shifts to companies that compound regardless

00:03:57.220 --> 00:03:59.220
and enter ROIC.

00:03:59.820 --> 00:04:04.840
Return on invested capital measures how efficiently a company turns capital into profits

00:04:04.840 --> 00:04:07.260
after accounting for the cost of that capital.

00:04:08.220 --> 00:04:12.940
In today's environment of constrained consumer spending and selective AI demand,

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:17.880
focusing on high ROIC businesses helps filter names that can compound

00:04:17.880 --> 00:04:20.020
even when macro data weakens.

00:04:20.700 --> 00:04:26.820
The approach starts with screening for companies posting ROIC above 15% over 5 years

00:04:26.820 --> 00:04:30.760
then checking free cash flow consistency and competitive positioning.

00:04:31.340 --> 00:04:35.880
Platforms such as wealth simple or quest trade allow investors to run these screens

00:04:35.880 --> 00:04:39.720
inside tax advantage to counts without additional software.

00:04:40.260 --> 00:04:43.960
Even strong domestic screens benefit from geographic ballast.

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:49.860
Diversification across developed Asian markets can protect against single-country policy risk

00:04:49.860 --> 00:04:55.120
when one market like Hong Kong's Hang Seng remains far below prior peaks

00:04:55.120 --> 00:05:02.340
due to property sector liabilities exceeding $300 billion and regulatory crackdowns on major tech names.

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:09.060
Today's conditions make this relevant because Japan's Nikkei, Taiwan's market and Korea's Cospi

00:05:09.060 --> 00:05:13.800
offer policy risk offsets while one market stays far below prior peaks.

00:05:14.420 --> 00:05:19.720
This reduces single-country concentration when one market stays far below prior peaks.

