00:09:04.220 --> 00:09:10.040
The win rate across simulated trades remains the key metric we track internally rather than any single outcome.

00:09:10.920 --> 00:09:16.140
Now here is something that most retail investors get wrong and it cost me money before I figured it out.

00:09:16.960 --> 00:09:23.540
Imagine you own shares in a bank that just beat earnings and raised its dividend yet the stock drifts lower on the day after.

00:09:24.540 --> 00:09:31.660
The mechanism is often post earnings profit taking by institutions that already modeled the capital markets revenue beat weeks earlier.

00:09:32.140 --> 00:09:37.300
The pro tip is to wait for volume to confirm the move rather than chasing the headline number.

00:09:37.940 --> 00:09:44.760
This separates informed entries from reactive ones and avoids the 11% style drawdown we saw with ACM.

